    {
      "line_range": "L57",
      "text": "`terraform.state.S3Reference` is a resource in the Pulumi terraform package that takes `bucket` and `key` arguments to reference Terraform state stored in S3.",
      "type": "api-surface",
      "source_hint": "@pulumi/terraform",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/get-started/terraform/next-steps.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L53-54",
      "text": "`pulumi.StackReference` takes a stack name and `getOutput` retrieves a stack output (e.g. \"core-infra\" stack's vpcId).",
      "type": "api-surface",
      "source_hint": "@pulumi/pulumi",
      "confidence": "low",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/get-started/terraform/next-steps.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L80",
      "text": "`S3Reference` exposes a `getOutput` method for reading Terraform state outputs.",
      "type": "api-surface",
      "source_hint": "@pulumi/terraform",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/get-started/terraform/next-steps.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L84-92",
      "text": "`aws.ecs.Cluster` accepts a `configuration.executeCommandConfiguration` argument with `kmsKeyId` and `logging` properties, with `logging: \"DEFAULT\"` a valid value.",
      "type": "api-surface",
      "source_hint": "pulumi/pulumi-aws",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/get-started/terraform/next-steps.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L101",
      "text": "`pulumi import` can be used to bring Terraform-managed resources under Pulumi management.",
      "type": "behavior",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/get-started/terraform/next-steps.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L103",
      "text": "Pulumi supports transferring state ownership gradually, resource-by-resource, from Terraform to Pulumi.",
      "type": "feature",
      "confidence": "low",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/get-started/terraform/next-steps.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L110-112",
      "text": "`pulumi import` accepts the syntax `pulumi import <type> <name> <id>`, e.g. `aws:ec2/vpc:Vpc main-vpc vpc-12345`, `aws:ec2/subnet:Subnet`, `aws:ecs/cluster:Cluster`.",
      "type": "api-surface",
      "confidence": "medium",
      "file": "content/docs/iac/get-started/terraform/next-steps.md",
      "found_by": [
        "llm-atomic"
      ]
    },
    {
      "line_range": "L126",
      "text": "`getOutput(\"resources\")` on a terraform S3Reference returns an array of resources that can be filtered and iterated, and a Pulumi import API exists to import resources programmatically.",
      "type": "api-surface",
      "confidence": "low",
